data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0d852574a0adead3016af25963ce9087d08447f32863c57311","output_index":8,"sequence_number":437,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Clarifying digit conditions**\n\nI’m considering a 5-digit number with strictly increasing digits. The first digit can’t be zero, and since it's a 5-digit number, leading zeroes are excluded by definition. So I’ll start with the first digit being at least one.\n\nThinking through the enumeration, I want to manually double-check my counts. It seems I can classify the remaining digits effectively, starting with the first digit at 1, 2, or 3, and then look at combinations for the rest. I’ll outline that as I go!"}

